{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And despite even this, when they are in the land of their enemies</b> etc. And what remained for Israel that they were not rejected and not abhorred? Were not all the good gifts given to them annulled from them? Rather, were it not for the Torah scrolls that remained for Israel, they would not differ from other nations at all. And upon this the liturgical poem was founded: ואין שיור רק התורה הזאת, 'and nothing remains but this Torah.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "ס״ת resolved as ספרי תורה (Torah scrolls); the cited piyyut line is rendered with a parenthetical gloss since the argument depends on identifying the phrase."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:43.773016330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}